commit=6aa48be1582e5c4ab260afbb50499b3eaad1aa04
date=2026-05-20
note=Audited at 6aa48be. Three layers of change since the previous stamp (fdfe289): (1) Pirkei Avot 1:11 sheet added with multi-sub-section pinned Mishnah (commits fac8f1a and 6aa48be). (2) Optional branching feature ("decision sections") added to the engine — sheets can now define `type: "decision"` sections with a `level`, `prompt`, and `branches[{id, label, blurb?, target}]`; targets are other sections that the engine hides until the matching branch is chosen at the right level. Path state lives in `?path=segment0/segment1`. On branching sheets the section-dots nav is replaced with a top-of-viewport breadcrumb. The closing-screen is also hidden until the path reaches a leaf, so an unanswered decision is a true scroll-stop. (3) `nasso-skeleton` content expanded from a stubbed 17-section tree to a fully-populated 22-section tree (4 themes × 3 leaves) distilled from Nechama Leibowitz's actual Nasso corpus (27 sheets). Themes reflect her real emphases: Gezel Hager, Nazir, Birkat Kohanim, Korban Hanesi'im. Sotah was dropped — she wrote zero sheets on it. Word-wrap on primary verses is now done synchronously inside `buildVerseContent` (rather than via requestAnimationFrame) so that headless / background-tab environments render highlights correctly. Backward compat preserved: linear sheets continue to render with section-dots and no path machinery.
